      "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/ig-ast-cache.svg",
      "description": "How an IG repository's own site is published, and how the AST it is built from is kept current (skill `ig-build-pipeline` §\"The AST cache lifecycle\").\n\nTHE RULE. An IG site is built from the IG Publisher AST read from the IG repository's cache branch `cat/fhir-harness/fhir-ast/<package id>`, never from Publisher HTML. The publish refuses an AST that is not valid for the commit it publishes (`ig-cache.sh restore` then `verify`). A later commit that changes no IG input (`sushi-config.yaml`, `ig.ini`, `input/`) does not make the AST stale.\n\nTHE REFRESH. The cache is written by ONE thing: fhir-harness's reusable workflow `.github/workflows/ig-ast-refresh.yml`, which an IG repository's Site publish calls as its first job (`ast`; template `templates/ig-repo-site/site-publish.yml`). It runs the Publisher through the AST exporter on a GitHub runner (Java, 10 GB heap, tx.fhir.org). It seeds the branch only from a commit on the default branch whose inputs equal the tip's.\n\nA valid AST is a cache, not a release: every page drawn from it carries the provisional mark (`ig-ast-delta`).",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "flowCount": 11,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/fhir-harness/directory/fhir-harness-processes",
      "name": "An IG site, built from the AST on its cache branch",
      "nodeCount": 11,
      "sourcePath": "processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/fhir-harness/blob/main/processes/content/ig-ast-cache.bpmn",
      "startNode": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/fhir-harness/process/Process_IgAstCache/node/Start_Publish",
      "summary": "How an IG repository's own site is published, and how the AST it is built from is kept current (skill `ig-build-pipeline` §\"The AST cache lifecycle\")."
